         - `yuv420p10` 10-bit HDR pixel format
         - `yuv422p10` 10-bit HDR pixel format
         - `yuv444p10` 10-bit HDR pixel format
         - `yuv420p12` 12-bit HDR pixel format
         - `yuv422p12` 12-bit HDR pixel format
         - `yuv444p12` 12-bit HDR pixel format
    preset : str, default is Undefined, optional
        Enforces the specified codec preset. The default is `veryfast`. The available options are [FFmpeg-compatible](https://trac.ffmpeg.org/wiki/Encode/H.265). Note that certain values for this field may cause the transcoder to override other fields you set in the `H265CodecSettings` message.
    profile : str, default is Undefined, optional
        Enforces the specified codec profile. The following profiles are
         supported:

         *   8-bit profiles
             *   `main` (default)
             *   `main-intra`
             *   `mainstillpicture`
         *   10-bit profiles
             *   `main10` (default)
             *   `main10-intra`
             *   `main422-10`
             *   `main422-10-intra`
             *   `main444-10`
             *   `main444-10-intra`
         *   12-bit profiles
             *   `main12` (default)
             *   `main12-intra`
             *   `main422-12`
             *   `main422-12-intra`
             *   `main444-12`
             *   `main444-12-intra`

         The available options are
         [FFmpeg-compatible](https://x265.readthedocs.io/).
         Note that certain values for this field may cause the
         transcoder to override other fields you set in the `H265CodecSettings`
         message.
    rateControlMode : str, default is Undefined, optional
        Specify the mode. The default is `vbr`.

         Supported rate control modes:

         - `vbr` - variable bitrate
         - `crf` - constant rate factor
    sdr : any, default is Undefined, optional
        Optional. SDR color format setting for H265.
    tune : str, default is Undefined, optional
        Enforces the specified codec tune. The available options are [FFmpeg-compatible](https://trac.ffmpeg.org/wiki/Encode/H.265). Note that certain values for this field may cause the transcoder to override other fields you set in the `H265CodecSettings` message.
    vbvFullnessBits : int, default is Undefined, optional
        Initial fullness of the Video Buffering Verifier (VBV) buffer in bits. Must be greater than zero. The default is equal to 90% of [H265CodecSettings.vbv_size_bits][google.cloud.video.transcoder.v1.VideoStream.H265CodecSettings.vbv_size_bits].
    vbvSizeBits : int, default is Undefined, optional
        Size of the Video Buffering Verifier (VBV) buffer in bits. Must be greater than zero. The default is equal to `VideoStream.bitrate_bps`.
    widthPixels : int, default is Undefined, optional
        The width of the video in pixels. Must be an even integer.
         When not specified, the width is adjusted to match the specified height
         and input aspect ratio. If both are omitted, the input width is used.

         For portrait videos that contain horizontal ASR and rotation metadata,
         provide the width, in pixels, per the horizontal ASR. The API calculates
         the height per the horizontal ASR. The API detects any rotation metadata
         and swaps the requested height and width for the output.
    """


    allowOpenGop?: bool

    aqStrength?: float

    bFrameCount?: int

    bPyramid?: bool

    bitrateBps?: int

    crfLevel?: int

    enableTwoPass?: bool

    frameRate?: float

    frameRateConversionStrategy?: str

    gopDuration?: str

    gopFrameCount?: int

    hdr10?: any

    heightPixels?: int

    hlg?: any

    pixelFormat?: str

    preset?: str

    profile?: str

    rateControlMode?: str

    sdr?: any

    tune?: str

    vbvFullnessBits?: int

    vbvSizeBits?: int

    widthPixels?: int


schema TranscoderCnrmCloudGoogleComV1alpha1TranscoderJobSpecConfigElementaryStreamsItems0VideoStreamVp9:
    r"""
    VP9 codec settings.

    Attributes
    ----------
    bitrateBps : int, default is Undefined, optional
        Required. The video bitrate in bits per second. The minimum value is 1,000. The maximum value is 480,000,000.
    crfLevel : int, default is Undefined, optional
        Target CRF level. Must be between 10 and 36, where 10 is the highest
         quality and 36 is the most efficient compression. The default is 21.

         **Note:** This field is not supported.
    frameRate : float, default is Undefined, optional
        Required. The target video frame rate in frames per second (FPS). Must be less than or equal to 120.
    frameRateConversionStrategy : str, default is Undefined, optional
        Optional. Frame rate conversion strategy for desired frame rate. The default is `DOWNSAMPLE`.
    gopDuration : str, default is Undefined, optional
        Select the GOP size based on the specified duration. The default is `3s`. Note that `gopDuration` must be less than or equal to [`segmentDuration`](#SegmentSettings), and [`segmentDuration`](#SegmentSettings) must be divisible by `gopDuration`.
    gopFrameCount : int, default is Undefined, optional
        Select the GOP size based on the specified frame count. Must be greater than zero.
    heightPixels : int, default is Undefined, optional
        The height of the video in pixels. Must be an even integer.
         When not specified, the height is adjusted to match the specified width
         and input aspect ratio. If both are omitted, the input height is used.

         For portrait videos that contain horizontal ASR and rotation metadata,
         provide the height, in pixels, per the horizontal ASR. The API calculates
         the width per the horizontal ASR. The API detects any rotation metadata
         and swaps the requested height and width for the output.
    hlg : any, default is Undefined, optional
        Optional. HLG color format setting for VP9.
    pixelFormat : str, default is Undefined, optional
        Pixel format to use. The default is `yuv420p`.

         Supported pixel formats:

         - `yuv420p` pixel format
         - `yuv422p` pixel format
         - `yuv444p` pixel format
         - `yuv420p10` 10-bit HDR pixel format
         - `yuv422p10` 10-bit HDR pixel format
         - `yuv444p10` 10-bit HDR pixel format
         - `yuv420p12` 12-bit HDR pixel format
         - `yuv422p12` 12-bit HDR pixel format
         - `yuv444p12` 12-bit HDR pixel format
    profile : str, default is Undefined, optional
        Enforces the specified codec profile. The following profiles are
         supported:

         *   `profile0` (default)
         *   `profile1`
         *   `profile2`
         *   `profile3`

         The available options are
         [WebM-compatible](https://www.webmproject.org/vp9/profiles/).
         Note that certain values for this field may cause the
         transcoder to override other fields you set in the `Vp9CodecSettings`
         message.
    rateControlMode : str, default is Undefined, optional
        Specify the mode. The default is `vbr`.

         Supported rate control modes:

         - `vbr` - variable bitrate
    sdr : any, default is Undefined, optional
        Optional. SDR color format setting for VP9.
    widthPixels : int, default is Undefined, optional
        The width of the video in pixels. Must be an even integer.
         When not specified, the width is adjusted to match the specified height
         and input aspect ratio. If both are omitted, the input width is used.

         For portrait videos that contain horizontal ASR and rotation metadata,
         provide the width, in pixels, per the horizontal ASR. The API calculates
         the height per the horizontal ASR. The API detects any rotation metadata
         and swaps the requested height and width for the output.
    """


